    }
  ],
  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan already plans Bitter Strength Gu as support beside All-out Effort Gu and self-reliance Gu when he locks his Shang clan city strength path set around All-out Effort Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          286
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_fang_yuan",
          "gu_self_reliance_gu",
          "loc_shang_clan_city",
          "gu_all_out_effort_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "He still lacks a copy then, and treats the Gu as expensive and rarely seen even in Shang clan city.",
        "chapters": [
          296
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Wei Yang warns that Shang Ya Zi, Shang Bi Xi, and Ju Kai Bei are the main rivals for that lot.",
        "chapters": [
          306
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "seeking-and-obtaining",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_wei_yang",
          "char_shang_ya_zi",
          "char_shang_bi_xi"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Shang Ya Zi later hands that same Gu to Fang Yuan as an apology while trying to salvage his young master position. Fang Yuan keeps it.",
        "chapters": [
          311
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "seeking-and-obtaining",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "In Northern Plains his second aperture still holds rank four Bitter Strength Gu, described again as increasing strength the more he is injured.",
        "chapters": [
          504
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "possession-and-myriad-self",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "reg_northern_plains"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "That Southern Border copy remains under Northern Plains region suppression, unlike his already advanced All-out Effort Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          516
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "possession-and-myriad-self",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "reg_southern_border"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Raising Bitter Strength Gu to rank five would be a huge project in materials and Gu worms; among Hei tribe goods he also finds further rank four Bitter Strength Gu for purchase rather than only refining his own upward.",
        "chapters": [
          517
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "possession-and-myriad-self",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_gu_worms",
          "fac_hei_tribe"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "These chapters do not state that he completes that rank five advance.",
        "chapters": [],
        "certainty": "inferred",
        "confidence": "C",
        "verification": "no_citation",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "possession-and-myriad-self",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "After he becomes a Gu Immortal, Bitter Strength Gu remains among the second aperture mortal Gu that form Myriad Self’s foundation beside rank four All-out Effort Gu and other strength Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          650
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "possession-and-myriad-self",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_gu_immortal",
          "sys_mortal_gu",
          "move_myriad_self",
          "gu_strength_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "When he uses immortal killer move Myriad Self, First Style, Giant Hand, the aperture again lists Bitter Strength Gu among the circling mortal Gu around Self Strength Immortal Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          782
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "possession-and-myriad-self",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "move_myriad_self_giant_hand",
          "gu_self_strength"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Even when Myriad Self’s core Immortal Gu are Self Strength, Pulling Mountain, Pulling Water, and Cleanse Soul, Bitter Strength Gu is still named among the supplementary mortal Gu for the full killer move.",
        "chapters": [
          1561
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
